accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  updated type  surgical pathology pathology report  ms 08  removed_accession_id  case  ms 08  removed_accession_id  removed_patient_name  date taken  removed_date source care unit  same day surgery  wacc 3 path subspecialty service  breast 2 results to  michele annette gadd  m d  signed out by  ronald balassanian  m d             addended report             reason for addendum  1  additional immunohistochemistry results reason for addendum  2  additional fluorescence in situ hybridization  fish  results reason for addendum  3  additional immunohistochemistry results clinical data  the patient is a 32 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer which is negative for er and pr and indeterminate for her 2neu by fish and ihc  a ct pet scan is only positive in the breast  she is undergoing planning for adjuvant therapy  a repeat her 2 neu with fish is requested on the core biopsy  final diagnosis  breast  left   core biopsy  poorly differentiated carcinoma  see note  note  sections of the core biopsy reveal an invasive tumor growing in sheets and large nests of tumor cells with associated desmoplasia  no tubule formation is present  a dense lymphoid infiltrate is also noted  there is only a small portion of normal uninvolved breast parenchyma present at one edge of the core biopsy  the tumor cells are large with abundant ill defined cytoplasm and have enlarged hyperchromatic nuclei with vesicular chromatin and prominent nucleoli  mitotic figures  including atypical forms are readily identified  the morphologic findings are those of a poorly differentiated carcinoma and in the context of the clinical presentation a breast primary is favored  to help exclude the possibility of metastasis from a different primary site  we performed a panel of immunoperoxidase stains on the core biopsy with the following results  immunostain target result vimentin renal  mesenchymal cells positive  removed_accession_id  renal cel